From: "adnan.drina" <adnan.drina@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 14:37:50 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 10/10] feat(transport): reserved-and-settled token accounting
 for the run allowance

RHOAI3 v15 (V15-1 change 2, tmp/v15-run-20260925/V15-1-DURABLE-QUOTA-
DESIGN.md section 3). With RHOAI3_ACCOUNTING_MODE=token the per-run
allowance is metered in tokens instead of requests, with no request-count
ceiling:

- Configuration (from the run's profile via the managed .env):
  RHOAI3_TOKEN_BUDGET=<B>/<window_seconds>, RHOAI3_TOKEN_RESERVATION=<C>
  (the served prompt+output bound), RHOAI3_REQUEST_LEDGER. Exactly one mode:
  mixed or incomplete settings, or C > B, raise AccountingConfigError and the
  process refuses before sending. Request mode (RHOAI3_REQUEST_BUDGET) is
  unchanged for runs pinned to it.
- Every physical HTTP attempt (main, retry, cap-boost retry, stream
  reconnect, sync/async auxiliary, gateway, reviewer) reserves C under the
  existing ledger lock and is admitted only if settled charges in the window
  plus all open reservations plus C <= B. The main-loop reservation and the
  transport hand-off consume the same reservation exactly once (the
  request-ownership PacedAttempt).
- Settlement: a settlement wrapper around chat.completions.create on the
  same client construction choke points settles each reservation exactly
  once at the terminal response to the validated provider usage
  (prompt+completion, consistent total, <= C); streams settle at the
  terminal chunk to the last usage record (cumulative frames are not
  summed). A terminal response without valid usage, or an HTTP error
  response, settles at C. An uncertain end (cancellation, crash, timeout,
  a stream that ended without its terminal chunk) writes nothing: the
  reservation stays open until reserved_at + hold + window, where hold
  (RHOAI3_TOKEN_RESERVATION_HOLD_SECONDS; default = the longest client
  request timeout this process honours, floor 900 s; a smaller explicit
  value is refused) must cover the longest a request can run: any upstream
  charge for it has then left the provider's own window too. Settled
  charges count for one full window after settlement. Duplicate settlements are ignored.
- Ledger lines: R <ts> <pid> <rid> <C> <label> / S <ts> <rid> <charge>
  <status>; state is reconstructed by reservation id.
- A token-mode request that reaches the transport without the settlement
  wiring is refused before sending (AccountingNotAttached).
- A full allowance defers through change 1's native path with
  accounting_mode=token and retry_not_before = when enough settled charge
  expires; when open reservations alone fill it, the deferral is marked
  uncertain with a bounded re-check time. The dispatcher's capacity check
  uses the same mode-aware peek.
