+
+Token mode (V15-1 change 2, RHOAI3_ACCOUNTING_MODE=token): instead of a
+request count, every physical HTTP attempt RESERVES ``C`` tokens
+(RHOAI3_TOKEN_RESERVATION, the served prompt+output bound) against a run
+allowance ``B`` per window (RHOAI3_TOKEN_BUDGET="<B>/<window_seconds>"),
+admitted only if ``settled_charges_in_window + unsettled_reservations + C <= B``
+under the ledger lock. After a valid terminal response the reservation is
+SETTLED exactly once to the validated provider usage (prompt+completion);
+a terminal response with missing/invalid usage settles at ``C``; an
+uncertain end (cancel, crash, broken stream, client timeout) keeps the full
+reservation unsettled until ``reserved_at + hold + window`` (hold =
+RHOAI3_TOKEN_RESERVATION_HOLD_SECONDS, default 900, at least the configured
+request timeout): any upstream charge for that request has left the
+provider's own window by then. Settled charges count for a full window after
+settlement. Ledger lines: ``R <ts> <pid> <rid> <C> <label>``
+and ``S <ts> <rid> <charge> <status>``. Exactly one mode per process;
+mixed or incomplete settings refuse before anything is sent.
